  "_doc": "DART tsunami buoys (columns A-L on the ops room wall). A quake triggers a buoy when its magnitude is at least trigger.min_mag and the buoy is within radius_km = radius_km_at_min_mag * radius_mult_per_mag ^ (mag - min_mag) of the hypocentre (200 km at M5.5, ~320 km at M6, ~790 km at M7). The buoy goes into event mode (red column) after the seismic waves reach it (distance / wave_speed_km_per_min) and stays there for event_mode_hours. lon is 0-360. POSITIONS ARE APPROXIMATE placeholders: edit them to match the real network.",

